  "ledger_annotations": [
    {
      "anchor": "  summary: Complete deterministic and live verification for the concurrent Story 4.8 AppHost-owned Dapr placement/scheduler path.\n",
      "inserted": "  status: done 2026-10-28\n  resolution: Superseded by removal of the active Works topology after historical Story 4.9 parity/rollback qualification. Current boundary and explicit-host-selection checks qualify replacement ownership; this closes the retired owned-path requirement, not separate live readiness findings. See [host-migration qualification](spec-five-deferred-host-migration-qualification.md).\n"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "  summary: Pin configuration- and policy-level Dapr ACL trust domains in the concurrent Story 4.8 topology tests.\n",
      "inserted": "  status: done 2026-10-28\n  resolution: The historical absence claim was already superseded by the concurrent-review audit. New parsed-YAML regressions pin all four selected Platform configurations and fixture copies: localhost control-plane trust, public workload/caller trust, and exact caller-policy counts. See [host-migration qualification](spec-five-deferred-host-migration-qualification.md).\n"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "  summary: Route the remaining live AppHost integration files through `WorksAppHostSmokeHarness` so the control-plane port settling repair covers every restart boundary.\n",
      "inserted": "  status: done 2026-10-28\n  resolution: The named legacy classes are retired. All six current live classes use the common harness; seven explicit facts require host selection, and focused harness controls qualify selected-port and owned-volume settling at startup and teardown. This does not close the separate control-plane-health race. See [host-migration qualification](spec-five-deferred-host-migration-qualification.md).\n"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "  summary: Resolve that the Release AppHost graph is not purely package-based because EventStore Operations is unpublishable.\n",
      "inserted": "  status: done 2026-10-28\n  resolution: Superseded by removal of the active Works AppHost and its Operations source edge. The evaluated current production executable has no external source edges in Release; intentional source-only Platform test adapters remain separately governed. See [host-migration qualification](spec-five-deferred-host-migration-qualification.md).\n"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "  summary: Make the transitional Works host pass the EventStore Story 5.5 startup route inventory, which sibling-source Debug builds already enforce.\n",
      "inserted": "  status: done 2026-10-28\n  resolution: The current thin SDK host passes actual startup and protected HTTP checks for named projection, event delivery and actor discovery. New negative controls prove unprotected canonical projection and sidecar-discovery endpoints fail the SDK startup inventory. See [host-migration qualification](spec-five-deferred-host-migration-qualification.md).\n"
    }
  ],
